  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 257 AM EDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\n- Scattered Showers and Isolated Storms This Morning\n\nRegional composite radar imagery shows convection developing \nassociated with a Low-level jet overrunning the stationary front to \nour south. The best coverage will be south, however rain showers are \npossible into this morning, especially south of I96. Instability is \npretty marginal but cannot rule out isolated storms. Conditions then \ndry out later today into Friday as high pressure takes over as the \nmain driver of our weather.\n\n- Heavy Rain Possible This Saturday\n\nOn the heels of this brief dry window comes widespread \nprecipitation Friday Night into Saturday. A ample southerly LLJ \nforces the front south of us back north as a warm front. In \nconjunction with marginal instability and PWATs near 2\" this is a \nfavorable setup for high rainfall efficiency. Some question based \non low placement and convective track as to where exactly the \nheaviest rain falls, however heavy rain is likely. High confidence\nin rainfall north of 1\" across much of the area, with NBM \nprobabilities of > 2\" north of 60% in spots. Overall the slight \nERO from WPC remains in good shape.",
